# ── THE SERVER'S VARIABLES, FOR `npm run dev` ────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill it in. `next dev` loads it into the
# Next.js server's environment, and the server renders /config.json from it exactly as the
# deployed container renders it from the task definition. The browser reads that document and
# nothing else; no value here is built into the bundle.
#
# THE SERVER REFUSES TO START when a required CONFIG_ variable or PORTAL_CSP_CONNECT_SRC is
# unset or empty, naming each one. An unset variable and an empty one are the same thing.
#
# ADDING A KEY MEANS TOUCHING FOUR PLACES, and only the first two are in this app:
#   1. the classification in apps/portal/src/types/runtimeConfig.types.ts, which the browser's
#      loader and the server's renderer both read
#   2. this file
#   3. its source — .github/config-outputs.json for a value Terraform computes, or a GitHub
#      Actions repository variable for a genuine input Terraform is given
#   4. the ECS task definition, which is two files: the infrastructure names the keys and their
#      values in one root map, and the module renders one CONFIG_<key> variable per entry —
#      derived, so no container can carry only some of them
# A test compares every leg, so a key wired in fewer than all of them fails CI rather than a
# deployment. It was five until the server began reading the browser's own classification.
#
# THE TEST SUITE DOES NOT READ THIS FILE. Under Vitest no server runs, and a test stubs a value
# with `vi.stubEnv('VITE_…')`, which lib/env.ts reads; those names are the test runner's alone.

# ── The API's origin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source: `tofu output -raw api_origin` from infra/ — a placeholder here, so copying this file
# does not point local dev at the production API with a real bearer.
# No trailing slash: every path is joined to it directly.
CONFIG_apiBaseUrl=https://api.your-domain.tld

# ── AWS Region ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source: `tofu output aws_region` from infra/
CONFIG_awsRegion=us-east-1

# ── Cognito ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source: `tofu output` from infra/ after apply: cognito_user_pool_id,
# cognito_user_pool_client_id and cognito_domain.
CONFIG_cognitoUserPoolId=us-east-1_XXXXXXXXX
CONFIG_cognitoUserPoolClientId=XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
CONFIG_cognitoDomain=your-domain.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com

# ── S3 Buckets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source: `tofu output s3_user_space_bucket_name` and the shared-space bucket's name.
CONFIG_userSpaceBucket=user-space-bucket-name
CONFIG_sharedSpaceBucket=shared-space-bucket-name

# ── Uploads ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Maximum single-file upload size in bytes. Optional — defaults to 5 GiB (5368709120) when
# unset. Files above this are rejected client-side before any request. Whether an upload is one
# PUT or multipart is the SERVER's decision, made from the file's size.
CONFIG_maxUploadBytes=5368709120

# ── Feature flags ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which block of config/feature-flags.json the browser resolves; the document's `environments`
# keys are the valid values — today, `prod`. Unset is safe — the app resolves the document's own
# `defaults` — but it silently ignores every per-environment override.
CONFIG_environment=prod

# ── App URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The origin Amplify sends the Hosted UI back to. `npm run dev` serves on port 5173, which
# Cognito's callback list and both buckets' CORS rules already admit.
CONFIG_appUrl=http://localhost:5173

# ── The CSP's connect-src ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every host the browser fetches: this origin, the Cognito User Pool endpoint, the Hosted UI
# domain (its token exchange is the one fetch a warm session never makes), both buckets and the
# API. Source: the `csp_connect_src` local in infra/main.tf.
#
# DOUBLE-QUOTE THE WHOLE VALUE. dotenv strips one pair of surrounding quotes, so `'self'` written
# bare in single quotes arrives as the host `self` and blocks every request, Next's own hot-reload
# socket included. Inside double quotes the single quotes survive.
PORTAL_CSP_CONNECT_SRC="'self' https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com https://your-domain.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com https://user-space-bucket-name.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com https://shared-space-bucket-name.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com https://api.your-domain.tld"
